  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday) \nIssued at 121 PM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nFriday night into Saturday an upper level trough will approach \nWest Central Texas from the west. This will bring our next chance \nof showers and thunderstorms to the area on Saturday. Low to \nmedium (20- 50%) rain chances are forecast across the area. Highs \non Saturday will be cooler due to the expected cloud cover and \npossibly rain. Highs will be in the mid to upper 60s with \novernight lows in the 50s. The next upper level trough is then \nforecast to dive southeast across the Southern Plains on late \nSaturday into Sunday. This will bring our next chance of rain \nSaturday night into Sunday. Low to medium (20-70%) rain chances \nare forecast for this time frame. Highs on Sunday will be in the \nupper 60s to near 70. \n\nA cold front will track south across the area Sunday night into \nMonday as the aforementioned upper level trough tracks east of the\nforecast area. Expect gusty north winds along with cooler \ntemperatures behind the front. Highs on Monday will be in the mid \n50s to near 60. Overnight lows will be in the 40s. The next upper \nlevel system may approach the area toward the middle of next week,\nwhich would bring our next chance of rainfall.",
